From 687997098357c1a3ac33be6fbeda51683fb02adb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:30:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FEX: signal frame done from the CPU after the copy's fence;
 see every GPU finish

vkd3d marks each Present() done on the frame done timeline with an empty
vkQueueSubmit2 right after vkQueuePresentKHR, holding the VkQueue that all
of the game's queues share. With Turnip on KGSL that submit took ~33 ms of
every frame in busy scenes (b61 log with VKD3D fex6: 'after present'
31-34 ms): it returned only once the GPU had finished the frame's copy into
the swapchain image. The copy and compute queues waited for the VkQueue
behind it, and the next frame's command lists only reached the GPU once it
had finished everything before.

The copy into the swapchain image now carries a VkFence. A frame done
thread waits for it, notes when the GPU finished, and signals the frame
done timeline with vkSignalSemaphore, so no empty submit is left and the
timeline never has a GPU-side point. Host waits for finished copies (before
reusing a swapchain image or an acquire semaphore) use what that thread
saw instead of waiting on the internal blit timeline.
VKD3D_FEX_HOST_FRAME_DONE=0 restores the empty submit.

Frame start pacing takes its GPU finish times from that thread, noted
before the frame done signal, so the wait worker always finds the finish of
the frame before. With the old GPU watcher the wait worker often looked
first (1-3 frames a second in fights); the spare formula then gave -10 to
-18 ms, which kept the hold-back at 0 for the next 64 frames. A frame whose
previous GPU finish still wasn't seen while the GPU finished it late now
leaves the hold-back alone (at most 8 in a row).

Diagnostics: a 'VkQueue lock' line (waits for the shared VkQueue, how long
holders kept it, holds of 5 ms or longer) and the frame done mode in the
present line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WLFWPd69Fe8cXrKbfompEp
