+
+    /* FEX frame done signal (VKD3D_FEX_HOST_FRAME_DONE, on unless 0; VKD3D fex7). vkd3d marks each Present() done on
+     * the frame done timeline (vk_complete_semaphore) with an empty vkQueueSubmit2 right after vkQueuePresentKHR,
+     * holding the VkQueue all of the game's queues share. Turnip on KGSL has no timeline semaphores of its own: Mesa
+     * emulates them and checks older points with a zero timeout, which KGSL takes as "wait forever". In busy scenes that
+     * submit sat ~33 ms of every frame in such a wait (b61 log with VKD3D fex6: 'after present' 31-34 ms), the copy and
+     * compute queues waited for the VkQueue behind it, and the next frame's command lists only reached the GPU once it
